    "statement": "\n    {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n    [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    (f : E → ℝ) (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f)\n    (hf2 : MemLp f 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))\n    (hgrad2 : MemLp (gradient f) 2 (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))\n    (hentropy : Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2))\n      (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)) :\n    let γ : Measure E := ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E\n    (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -\n      (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) ≤\n      2 * ∫ x, ‖gradient f x‖^2 ∂γ",
    "statement_sha256": "f905ed6ba2b029fec432b394b87220c134e2d54b5977d64b36fcb8f76cb11a16",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "For every finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space E equipped with its compatible norm and Borel measurable structure, including dimension zero, let gamma be the canonical centered Gaussian measure with variance one in each orthonormal coordinate. For every signed real-valued function f on E which is globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable, assume f and its literal global gradient are genuinely in L2(gamma), and assume x -> f(x)^2 log(f(x)^2) is integrable with respect to gamma. Then\nintegral f(x)^2 log(f(x)^2) dgamma - (integral f(x)^2 dgamma) log(integral f(x)^2 dgamma) <= 2 integral ||gradient f(x)||^2 dgamma.\nThe gradient is the Riesz representation of the real Frechet derivative and the norm is the Hilbert norm. All integrals are real Bochner integrals; log is totalized at zero and the product t log t is interpreted continuously at t=0. The assertion requires no positivity of f or of its square mass, and no normalization, compact support, additional cutoff limit, or inequality certificate.",
    "text_sha256": "281c97502ff8201c939167953dae58ad987c5fa02e995adfc9c5f814f1cf493a",
    "decoder": "blind_statement_decoder_42",
